  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/6C5BA3">Definition <span data-tag="6C5BA3">1.1.3.2</span>.</a>homotopy category!of a topological category Let $\calC $ be a topological category. The <em>homotopy category</em> $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ is defined as follows:hcalC@$\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li><p>
The objects of $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ are the objects of $\calC $. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
If $X,Y \in \calC $, then we define $\Hom _{\rm {h} \it {\calC }}(X,Y)= \pi _0 \bHom _{\calC }(X,Y)$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Composition of morphisms in $\rm {h} \it {\calC }$ is induced from the composition of morphisms in $\calC $ by applying the functor $\pi _0$. 
</p>
</li>
</ul></p>
